1
00:00:00,290 --> 00:00:01,520
If your knee replacement

2
00:00:01,520 --> 00:00:03,300
still hurts and the X-ray

3
00:00:03,300 --> 00:00:04,850
keeps coming back fine,

4
00:00:04,850 --> 00:00:05,820
don't accept that.

5
00:00:06,480 --> 00:00:07,630
I've been driving a
delivery

6
00:00:07,630 --> 00:00:08,940
truck for thirty years.

7
00:00:08,940 --> 00:00:09,880
In and out of the truck

8
00:00:09,880 --> 00:00:11,070
and up and down porch
steps,

9
00:00:11,070 --> 00:00:12,760
hundreds of times a day.

10
00:00:12,760 --> 00:00:13,440
I had my right

11
00:00:13,440 --> 00:00:15,120
knee replaced two years
ago.

12
00:00:15,540 --> 00:00:17,260
It has hurt every day
since.

13
00:00:17,260 --> 00:00:18,910
Not surgery pain.

14
00:00:18,910 --> 00:00:20,540
I know what that felt like,

15
00:00:20,540 --> 00:00:21,530
and it went away.

16
00:00:21,530 --> 00:00:22,720
This is different.

17
00:00:22,720 --> 00:00:23,110
Tight.

18
00:00:23,110 --> 00:00:23,830
Full.

19
00:00:23,830 --> 00:00:24,800
Like a band around

20
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:26,900
the joint that never
loosens.

21
00:00:26,900 --> 00:00:28,650
And for two years I've

22
00:00:28,650 --> 00:00:29,970
been told the same thing.

23
00:00:30,540 --> 00:00:31,620
Give it time.

24
00:00:31,620 --> 00:00:33,950
At six weeks it was
swelling,

25
00:00:33,950 --> 00:00:35,520
and swelling is normal.

26
00:00:35,520 --> 00:00:37,700
At three months, give it
six.

27
00:00:37,700 --> 00:00:38,670
At six months,

28
00:00:38,670 --> 00:00:40,390
some knees take a full
year.

29
00:00:40,390 --> 00:00:41,120
At a year,

30
00:00:41,120 --> 00:00:42,920
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

31
00:00:43,280 --> 00:00:44,740
And I didn't just wait.

32
00:00:44,740 --> 00:00:46,120
We went down the list.

33
00:00:46,120 --> 00:00:47,680
More physical therapy.

34
00:00:47,680 --> 00:00:50,190
Every session, every
exercise at home.

35
00:00:50,190 --> 00:00:51,330
I got stronger.

36
00:00:51,330 --> 00:00:52,590
The tightness never
moved.

37
00:00:52,590 --> 00:00:54,130
The pain pills helped,

38
00:00:54,130 --> 00:00:55,190
and that was the problem.

39
00:00:55,600 --> 00:00:57,560
I'm already on enough
every morning,

40
00:00:57,560 --> 00:00:58,650
and nobody could tell me

41
00:00:58,650 --> 00:00:59,780
when I'd get to stop.

42
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:01,840
Then a nerve block.

43
00:01:01,840 --> 00:01:03,520
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

44
00:01:03,520 --> 00:01:04,230
And after that,

45
00:01:04,230 --> 00:01:05,520
a second operation to go

46
00:01:05,520 --> 00:01:07,290
back in and do it over.

47
00:01:07,290 --> 00:01:08,340
I said no.

48
00:01:08,340 --> 00:01:09,820
Every morning I stepped
out

49
00:01:09,820 --> 00:01:11,270
of bed and my knee

50
00:01:11,270 --> 00:01:12,320
felt like a band

51
00:01:12,320 --> 00:01:13,760
was wrapped around it,

52
00:01:13,760 --> 00:01:15,920
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

53
00:01:16,330 --> 00:01:17,630
Every morning I took
something

54
00:01:17,630 --> 00:01:19,500
for it and ran my route.

55
00:01:19,500 --> 00:01:20,860
Couldn't do the stairs,

56
00:01:20,860 --> 00:01:21,900
couldn't stand at the
counter

57
00:01:21,900 --> 00:01:23,640
long enough to finish
dinner,

58
00:01:23,640 --> 00:01:25,400
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's game

59
00:01:25,400 --> 00:01:27,360
without shifting every two
minutes.

60
00:01:27,360 --> 00:01:28,260
On my route,

61
00:01:28,260 --> 00:01:29,740
I'd park closer and closer

62
00:01:29,740 --> 00:01:30,760
to every door just

63
00:01:30,760 --> 00:01:32,270
to save a few steps.

64
00:01:32,270 --> 00:01:33,840
It woke me at night,

65
00:01:33,840 --> 00:01:36,220
and it turned ordinary
things,

66
00:01:36,220 --> 00:01:38,100
like climbing up into the
truck

67
00:01:38,100 --> 00:01:39,740
or up off the couch,

68
00:01:39,740 --> 00:01:40,820
into a decision.

69
00:01:41,580 --> 00:01:43,080
After a long and serious

70
00:01:43,080 --> 00:01:44,530
talk with my wife,

71
00:01:44,530 --> 00:01:46,450
I went back in one more
time.

72
00:01:46,800 --> 00:01:48,010
That was the fourth set

73
00:01:48,010 --> 00:01:49,810
of X-rays on this knee.

74
00:01:49,810 --> 00:01:51,120
And like the three before
it,

75
00:01:51,120 --> 00:01:53,610
the answer was everything
looks great.

76
00:01:53,610 --> 00:01:55,990
No loosening, no infection,
nothing wrong.

77
00:01:56,400 --> 00:01:57,640
Only this time

78
00:01:57,640 --> 00:01:59,130
there was no new number.

79
00:01:59,130 --> 00:02:01,720
Nobody said give it
another six months.

80
00:02:01,720 --> 00:02:03,260
There was nothing left to
give it.

81
00:02:03,660 --> 00:02:04,500
I sat in the parking

82
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:05,700
lot for a while.

83
00:02:05,700 --> 00:02:06,990
Okay, I thought.

84
00:02:06,990 --> 00:02:08,060
Then explain this.

85
00:02:08,470 --> 00:02:10,580
Anyway, a couple of
months back,

86
00:02:10,580 --> 00:02:11,980
I hit my breaking point.

87
00:02:12,370 --> 00:02:14,630
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

88
00:02:14,630 --> 00:02:15,590
Everyone in the house

89
00:02:15,590 --> 00:02:17,720
was asleep and I was
downstairs

90
00:02:17,720 --> 00:02:19,460
in the recliner with my leg
up,

91
00:02:19,460 --> 00:02:20,540
trying to find any

92
00:02:20,540 --> 00:02:21,700
angle where it didn't feel

93
00:02:21,700 --> 00:02:23,010
like something was
wrapped around

94
00:02:23,010 --> 00:02:24,660
my knee and tightening.

95
00:02:25,110 --> 00:02:27,520
My wife didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

96
00:02:27,520 --> 00:02:29,460
By then I'd stopped telling
her.

97
00:02:29,460 --> 00:02:30,120
I had a route

98
00:02:30,120 --> 00:02:31,390
to start at seven.

99
00:02:31,390 --> 00:02:32,340
And I just thought,

100
00:02:32,340 --> 00:02:34,280
is this really my life now?

101
00:02:34,280 --> 00:02:35,980
I can't live like this.

102
00:02:35,980 --> 00:02:37,460
Thirty years on the route,

103
00:02:37,460 --> 00:02:38,440
and I couldn't see how

104
00:02:38,440 --> 00:02:40,230
I'd climb one more porch.

105
00:02:40,230 --> 00:02:42,130
So I made myself a
promise.

106
00:02:42,130 --> 00:02:42,940
I wouldn't go a day

107
00:02:42,940 --> 00:02:44,360
without looking for an
answer.

108
00:02:44,360 --> 00:02:45,610
And when I found one,

109
00:02:45,610 --> 00:02:46,690
I'd share it with everyone

110
00:02:46,690 --> 00:02:48,070
going through the same
thing.

111
00:02:48,070 --> 00:02:49,030
So I got my laptop

112
00:02:49,030 --> 00:02:50,400
out and went looking.

113
00:02:50,400 --> 00:02:51,640
Not for a product.

114
00:02:51,640 --> 00:02:52,690
For an explanation.

115
00:02:53,110 --> 00:02:54,930
Mayo Clinic forums,

116
00:02:54,930 --> 00:02:57,460
the knee replacement
group on Facebook,

117
00:02:57,460 --> 00:03:00,340
doctor videos, medical
animations.

118
00:03:00,720 --> 00:03:01,770
And that's when I found

119
00:03:01,770 --> 00:03:03,120
a video from a physical

120
00:03:03,120 --> 00:03:04,810
therapist named Dr.

121
00:03:04,810 --> 00:03:07,460
Steven Salinger, whose
own wife

122
00:03:07,460 --> 00:03:09,500
had been through exactly
this.

123
00:03:09,500 --> 00:03:11,300
But before I say anything
else,

124
00:03:11,300 --> 00:03:12,590
I want to be straight with
you.

125
00:03:13,100 --> 00:03:15,340
You've already had
something work fast.

126
00:03:15,340 --> 00:03:16,390
The ice.

127
00:03:16,390 --> 00:03:18,160
The first week of a new
pill.

128
00:03:18,160 --> 00:03:19,900
The good day after a
session.

129
00:03:19,900 --> 00:03:20,850
Then it wore off.

130
00:03:20,850 --> 00:03:22,940
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

131
00:03:23,330 --> 00:03:25,540
Fast relief isn't relief.

132
00:03:25,540 --> 00:03:26,480
It's a preview.

133
00:03:26,840 --> 00:03:27,720
So I'm not going

134
00:03:27,720 --> 00:03:29,630
to tell you this works fast.

135
00:03:29,630 --> 00:03:30,810
It doesn't.

136
00:03:30,810 --> 00:03:32,540
But if you're willing to be
patient,

137
00:03:32,540 --> 00:03:33,360
and to look at what's

138
00:03:33,360 --> 00:03:34,560
going on around your new

139
00:03:34,560 --> 00:03:36,520
knee instead of inside it,

140
00:03:36,520 --> 00:03:37,240
there is a real

141
00:03:37,240 --> 00:03:39,080
reason it still hurts.

142
00:03:39,080 --> 00:03:41,690
And something you can do
about it.

143
00:03:41,690 --> 00:03:43,370
Let me explain what he
said,

144
00:03:43,370 --> 00:03:44,330
because this is what

145
00:03:44,330 --> 00:03:46,390
changed everything for
me.

146
00:03:46,390 --> 00:03:48,500
He started with the basics.

147
00:03:48,500 --> 00:03:49,840
A knee replacement takes

148
00:03:49,840 --> 00:03:51,850
out the worn joint surfaces

149
00:03:51,850 --> 00:03:53,920
and puts in metal and
plastic.

150
00:03:53,920 --> 00:03:55,770
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

151
00:03:55,770 --> 00:03:57,350
you had before the
operation.

152
00:03:57,770 --> 00:03:59,300
That part I already knew.

153
00:03:59,700 --> 00:04:01,070
But then he explained
something

154
00:04:01,070 --> 00:04:02,710
nobody had ever told me.

155
00:04:03,070 --> 00:04:04,080
He said, think about

156
00:04:04,080 --> 00:04:06,470
a swollen foot inside a
shoe.

157
00:04:06,470 --> 00:04:08,070
The shoe didn't shrink.

158
00:04:08,070 --> 00:04:08,960
Your foot is taking

159
00:04:08,960 --> 00:04:11,120
up more room, so
everything feels

160
00:04:11,120 --> 00:04:13,200
cramped and tight and
squeezed.

161
00:04:13,200 --> 00:04:14,230
Your new knee sits

162
00:04:14,230 --> 00:04:15,760
in a limited space with
living

163
00:04:15,760 --> 00:04:17,520
tissue packed all around
it.

164
00:04:17,970 --> 00:04:19,020
To put that knee in,

165
00:04:19,020 --> 00:04:19,870
the surgeon had

166
00:04:19,870 --> 00:04:21,220
to work through that
tissue.

167
00:04:21,580 --> 00:04:24,110
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

168
00:04:24,110 --> 00:04:25,720
At first that's normal.

169
00:04:25,720 --> 00:04:26,710
But in some people

170
00:04:26,710 --> 00:04:28,230
that swelling can stay
switched

171
00:04:28,230 --> 00:04:30,420
on far longer than
expected.

172
00:04:30,420 --> 00:04:32,120
And swollen tissue takes
up more

173
00:04:32,120 --> 00:04:34,140
room than calm tissue
does.

174
00:04:34,140 --> 00:04:35,980
So when you bend,

175
00:04:36,350 --> 00:04:38,540
that tissue gets
compressed.

176
00:04:38,540 --> 00:04:39,980
When you straighten,

177
00:04:39,980 --> 00:04:41,490
it gets pulled tight.

178
00:04:41,490 --> 00:04:42,710
That's the band.

179
00:04:42,710 --> 00:04:45,530
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

180
00:04:45,530 --> 00:04:46,430
And you start being

181
00:04:46,430 --> 00:04:47,490
the one who says,

182
00:04:47,490 --> 00:04:48,290
you go ahead.

183
00:04:48,290 --> 00:04:49,590
I'll stay here.

184
00:04:49,590 --> 00:04:50,530
And that's exactly why

185
00:04:50,530 --> 00:04:51,290
so much of what

186
00:04:51,290 --> 00:04:52,820
I'd tried hadn't worked.

187
00:04:52,820 --> 00:04:54,930
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

188
00:04:54,930 --> 00:04:55,970
around the knee.

189
00:04:55,970 --> 00:04:57,990
Worth doing, and I'd done
it.

190
00:04:57,990 --> 00:04:59,090
It does nothing about

191
00:04:59,090 --> 00:05:00,660
tissue taking up room.

192
00:05:00,660 --> 00:05:01,880
A nerve block quiets

193
00:05:01,880 --> 00:05:03,720
the nerve carrying the
signal.

194
00:05:03,720 --> 00:05:05,860
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

195
00:05:06,320 --> 00:05:07,550
But when that irritated

196
00:05:07,550 --> 00:05:09,690
tissue finally calms down,

197
00:05:09,690 --> 00:05:11,370
it holds less fluid,

198
00:05:11,370 --> 00:05:12,960
and it takes up less room.

199
00:05:13,400 --> 00:05:14,960
Less room taken up means

200
00:05:14,960 --> 00:05:17,160
less pressure squeezing
the joint.

201
00:05:17,160 --> 00:05:18,930
That's what takes the
pressure off.

202
00:05:19,310 --> 00:05:20,810
After two years of this,

203
00:05:20,810 --> 00:05:22,340
it finally made sense.

204
00:05:22,740 --> 00:05:24,810
The problem was never
the new knee.

205
00:05:24,810 --> 00:05:26,660
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

206
00:05:27,070 --> 00:05:28,700
He calls it the squeeze.

207
00:05:28,700 --> 00:05:30,090
Once you've felt it,

208
00:05:30,090 --> 00:05:31,070
that's the word.

209
00:05:31,420 --> 00:05:34,490
I'd bought knee sleeves,
compression braces,

210
00:05:34,490 --> 00:05:37,000
creams, half of Amazon
really,

211
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:38,030
and all any of it

212
00:05:38,030 --> 00:05:39,270
gave me was an hour.

213
00:05:39,660 --> 00:05:40,730
I even looked at going

214
00:05:40,730 --> 00:05:42,690
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

215
00:05:42,690 --> 00:05:44,780
But at $200 a session

216
00:05:44,780 --> 00:05:46,580
with nothing covered by
insurance,

217
00:05:46,580 --> 00:05:47,920
that was a quick no.

218
00:05:47,920 --> 00:05:49,040
Then one night I went

219
00:05:49,040 --> 00:05:50,310
back to that knee
replacement

220
00:05:50,310 --> 00:05:52,060
group and actually read it.

221
00:05:52,060 --> 00:05:53,380
Thousands of people,

222
00:05:53,380 --> 00:05:55,020
years out from surgery,

223
00:05:55,020 --> 00:05:56,430
comparing notes on
stiffness

224
00:05:56,430 --> 00:05:58,620
and tightness nobody
could explain.

225
00:05:59,060 --> 00:06:00,800
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

226
00:06:00,800 --> 00:06:02,600
the same thing kept
coming up.

227
00:06:02,600 --> 00:06:05,070
This one device, and
people

228
00:06:05,070 --> 00:06:06,120
saying it was the first

229
00:06:06,120 --> 00:06:07,440
thing that made a
difference.

230
00:06:07,820 --> 00:06:10,020
And before anyone jumps
in thinking,

231
00:06:10,020 --> 00:06:11,350
alright, here it comes,

232
00:06:11,350 --> 00:06:12,690
he's selling me something,

233
00:06:12,690 --> 00:06:14,540
let me shut that down
right now.

234
00:06:14,540 --> 00:06:15,350
I'm only here because

235
00:06:15,350 --> 00:06:16,540
I made myself a promise

236
00:06:16,540 --> 00:06:18,030
at 2:30 in the morning

237
00:06:18,030 --> 00:06:18,990
that if I ever found

238
00:06:18,990 --> 00:06:21,070
something that helped, I'd
say so.

239
00:06:21,740 --> 00:06:23,260
It's called the KenRelief

240
00:06:23,260 --> 00:06:25,140
Red Light Therapy Wrap.

241
00:06:25,140 --> 00:06:27,250
At first glance I didn't buy
it.

242
00:06:27,250 --> 00:06:28,360
It looked like the cheap

243
00:06:28,360 --> 00:06:30,150
knee sleeves off Amazon

244
00:06:30,150 --> 00:06:31,900
that did nothing for me.

245
00:06:31,900 --> 00:06:33,870
But I went to their website
anyway,

246
00:06:33,870 --> 00:06:34,620
just to see what

247
00:06:34,620 --> 00:06:35,760
all the fuss was about.

248
00:06:36,180 --> 00:06:37,220
It's the same red

249
00:06:37,220 --> 00:06:39,510
light therapy clinics
charge $200

250
00:06:39,510 --> 00:06:41,680
a session for, off machines

251
00:06:41,680 --> 00:06:43,710
that cost fifty thousand
dollars,

252
00:06:43,710 --> 00:06:44,770
in a wrap you plug

253
00:06:44,770 --> 00:06:46,260
into the wall at home.

254
00:06:46,260 --> 00:06:48,090
Two hundred and forty
lights.

255
00:06:48,090 --> 00:06:50,230
Red at 660 nanometers

256
00:06:50,600 --> 00:06:53,270
and near-infrared at 850,

257
00:06:53,270 --> 00:06:55,770
run together for the
strongest effect.

258
00:06:55,770 --> 00:06:57,390
Four strength levels.

259
00:06:57,390 --> 00:06:59,320
A five to thirty minute
timer.

260
00:06:59,320 --> 00:07:00,910
Then I saw the guarantee.

261
00:07:00,910 --> 00:07:02,150
Ninety days.

262
00:07:02,150 --> 00:07:04,040
Results or your money
back,

263
00:07:04,040 --> 00:07:06,610
no questions, no store
credit,

264
00:07:06,610 --> 00:07:08,580
and you don't even send it
back.

265
00:07:08,580 --> 00:07:10,610
No physical therapist ever
gave me

266
00:07:10,610 --> 00:07:12,760
ninety days to change my
mind.

267
00:07:12,760 --> 00:07:14,200
There wasn't much to lose,

268
00:07:14,200 --> 00:07:15,280
so I ordered it.

269
00:07:15,280 --> 00:07:16,710
Two of them, actually.

270
00:07:16,710 --> 00:07:18,800
Only the right knee was
replaced,

271
00:07:18,800 --> 00:07:19,930
but you favor the leg

272
00:07:19,930 --> 00:07:21,470
that hurts, and I'd done

273
00:07:21,470 --> 00:07:22,660
it for two years.

274
00:07:22,660 --> 00:07:24,810
The left one was carrying
the difference.

275
00:07:24,810 --> 00:07:25,420
When it came,

276
00:07:25,420 --> 00:07:27,440
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

277
00:07:27,440 --> 00:07:28,530
because I'd been let down

278
00:07:28,530 --> 00:07:30,630
too many times to get
excited.

279
00:07:30,630 --> 00:07:32,630
What I felt was warmth.

280
00:07:32,630 --> 00:07:34,760
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

281
00:07:34,760 --> 00:07:35,880
More like it was coming

282
00:07:35,880 --> 00:07:37,000
from inside the knee

283
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:38,550
and spreading around it.

284
00:07:38,550 --> 00:07:39,530
And that was it.

285
00:07:39,530 --> 00:07:41,230
That was the whole
experience.

286
00:07:41,230 --> 00:07:42,380
When I took it off,

287
00:07:42,380 --> 00:07:43,490
I'll be honest,

288
00:07:43,490 --> 00:07:45,470
nothing dramatic had
happened.

289
00:07:45,470 --> 00:07:47,150
And after what that video
said,

290
00:07:47,150 --> 00:07:49,230
that's exactly what I
expected.

291
00:07:49,620 --> 00:07:50,330
What was different

292
00:07:50,330 --> 00:07:51,680
was that for the first

293
00:07:51,680 --> 00:07:53,560
time in two years I'd done

294
00:07:53,560 --> 00:07:54,810
something for my knee

295
00:07:54,810 --> 00:07:55,840
instead of to it.

296
00:07:56,210 --> 00:07:58,390
Twenty minutes, in my
own chair,

297
00:07:58,390 --> 00:07:59,650
after my route.

298
00:07:59,650 --> 00:08:01,910
No drive, no copay.

299
00:08:01,910 --> 00:08:03,110
They say twenty minutes.

300
00:08:03,470 --> 00:08:05,650
I did thirty, twice a day,

301
00:08:05,650 --> 00:08:07,650
lowest setting that first
week.

302
00:08:07,650 --> 00:08:08,950
I put it on the calendar.

303
00:08:08,950 --> 00:08:09,980
The first week,

304
00:08:09,980 --> 00:08:10,840
I couldn't have told

305
00:08:10,840 --> 00:08:12,690
you if anything was
happening.

306
00:08:12,690 --> 00:08:13,450
I tried not

307
00:08:13,450 --> 00:08:14,450
to get my hopes up.

308
00:08:14,830 --> 00:08:15,620
I'd had things help

309
00:08:15,620 --> 00:08:17,430
for a week and then stop.

310
00:08:17,780 --> 00:08:19,160
But somewhere in the
second week

311
00:08:19,160 --> 00:08:20,300
I noticed I'd come down

312
00:08:20,300 --> 00:08:22,030
the stairs without holding
the rail.

313
00:08:22,420 --> 00:08:23,740
I hadn't decided to.

314
00:08:23,740 --> 00:08:24,790
I just did it,

315
00:08:24,790 --> 00:08:27,740
then stopped halfway
down because I realized.

316
00:08:27,740 --> 00:08:28,720
By the end of the fourth

317
00:08:28,720 --> 00:08:29,820
week I'd slept through

318
00:08:29,820 --> 00:08:31,760
the night four times
running.

319
00:08:32,110 --> 00:08:33,050
I stood at the counter

320
00:08:33,050 --> 00:08:34,350
and finished making
dinner without

321
00:08:34,350 --> 00:08:35,520
looking for the stool.

322
00:08:35,890 --> 00:08:37,310
None of that is dramatic.

323
00:08:37,310 --> 00:08:37,720
All of it

324
00:08:37,720 --> 00:08:39,580
was gone for two years.

325
00:08:39,580 --> 00:08:40,900
A few weeks later my wife

326
00:08:40,900 --> 00:08:42,190
asked if I wanted to walk

327
00:08:42,190 --> 00:08:43,970
the long way around the
block.

328
00:08:43,970 --> 00:08:45,050
And for the first time

329
00:08:45,050 --> 00:08:46,910
in two years, I said yes.

330
00:08:46,910 --> 00:08:48,960
I wanted to understand
why,

331
00:08:48,960 --> 00:08:50,700
so I read the whole thing.

332
00:08:50,700 --> 00:08:52,650
It comes down to four
steps.

333
00:08:52,650 --> 00:08:53,600
One.

334
00:08:53,600 --> 00:08:54,990
The tissue around a new

335
00:08:54,990 --> 00:08:56,980
knee can stay inflamed

336
00:08:56,980 --> 00:08:59,220
long after surgery is over.

337
00:08:59,600 --> 00:09:00,590
Two.

338
00:09:00,590 --> 00:09:03,210
Inflamed tissue holds
extra fluid,

339
00:09:03,210 --> 00:09:04,120
so it takes up more

340
00:09:04,120 --> 00:09:05,390
room than it should.

341
00:09:05,390 --> 00:09:06,030
Three.

342
00:09:06,030 --> 00:09:07,840
There's only so much room
in there.

343
00:09:07,840 --> 00:09:09,370
Bending compresses it.

344
00:09:09,370 --> 00:09:11,330
Straightening pulls it
tight.

345
00:09:11,330 --> 00:09:12,730
That's the squeeze.

346
00:09:12,730 --> 00:09:13,510
Four.

347
00:09:14,040 --> 00:09:15,840
Red and near-infrared
light have

348
00:09:15,840 --> 00:09:17,810
been studied for calming
that inflammation,

349
00:09:17,810 --> 00:09:19,160
so the swelling and the
pressure

350
00:09:19,160 --> 00:09:20,540
can come down with it.

351
00:09:20,540 --> 00:09:22,120
In a randomized trial,

352
00:09:22,120 --> 00:09:24,110
patients given light
therapy after

353
00:09:24,110 --> 00:09:26,430
a knee replacement had
less pain,

354
00:09:26,430 --> 00:09:28,240
less swelling and better
early

355
00:09:28,240 --> 00:09:29,810
movement than those who
weren't.

356
00:09:30,240 --> 00:09:32,640
A 2025 review said the
same,

357
00:09:32,640 --> 00:09:33,260
and was clear

358
00:09:33,260 --> 00:09:35,100
the evidence is still
limited.

359
00:09:35,100 --> 00:09:37,200
I probably sound like a
broken

360
00:09:37,200 --> 00:09:38,980
record to my family

361
00:09:38,980 --> 00:09:40,590
and the folks on my route.

362
00:09:40,970 --> 00:09:42,930
But after two years of
doing everything

363
00:09:42,930 --> 00:09:45,360
I was told and getting
nowhere,

364
00:09:45,360 --> 00:09:46,540
you have no idea what

365
00:09:46,540 --> 00:09:48,360
it's like to sleep through
the night,

366
00:09:48,360 --> 00:09:49,850
say yes to the walk,

367
00:09:49,850 --> 00:09:51,270
and get my life back.

368
00:09:51,270 --> 00:09:52,750
So take it from me.

369
00:09:52,750 --> 00:09:53,970
Don't spend another year

370
00:09:53,970 --> 00:09:55,620
waiting for it to settle.

371
00:09:55,620 --> 00:09:57,700
Don't spend two hundred a
session.

372
00:09:57,700 --> 00:09:59,250
More than ten thousand
people

373
00:09:59,250 --> 00:10:00,320
with pain after a knee

374
00:10:00,320 --> 00:10:02,480
replacement have already
tried this.

375
00:10:02,480 --> 00:10:04,300
Some had it worse than I
did.

376
00:10:04,300 --> 00:10:05,460
You can get the KenRelief

377
00:10:05,460 --> 00:10:07,060
wrap from their website,

378
00:10:07,060 --> 00:10:08,010
